1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,520
The Rebrand I Wish I Could Redo.

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:06,600
Last year, I worked on a rebranding project for a small coffee company.

3
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:10,440
Looking back, I wish I had listened to my instincts from the beginning.  

4
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:13,000
If I had asked more questions in the first meeting,

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,520
I would have understood what the client really wanted.

6
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:19,840
Instead, I opened Illustrator and designed a logo in two days.

7
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:22,880
When I presented it, the client looked confused.

8
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:26,360
"It's beautiful,". she said,

9
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:28,040
"but it doesn't feel like us.".

10
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:29,960
"What do you mean?" I asked.

11
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:34,360
"If you had visited our shop, you would have seen that we are warm and old-fashioned.

12
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:37,000
This design looks cold and modern.".

13
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,680
I felt terrible.

14
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,600
If only I had spent one afternoon in her shop,

15
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:43,840
I would have saved us all a lot of time.

16
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:47,160
Without a proper brief, I had worked completely in the dark.

17
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:50,400
I had even chosen the colors without checking her brand guidelines.

18
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:52,080
I should have asked for them first,

19
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:54,600
otherwise the colors would never match her packaging,

20
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:56,280
and of course they didn't.

21
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:58,880
That evening, I called my colleague Deniz. 

22
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:01,640
"I wish I hadn't rushed," I told him.

23
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:04,680
"Don't be so hard on yourself,". he said.

24
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:07,000
“But you should have shown her some sketches first.

25
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,880
If you had shared early ideas,

26
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:12,920
she could have corrected you before you spent two days on the final file.".

27
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:13,880
"I know.

28
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:15,760
I wish I had been more patient.".

29
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:17,120
"Well, it's not too late.

30
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:18,400
Let's fix it together.".

31
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:20,200
We worked all weekend.

32
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:22,880
But for Deniz, I would have missed the new deadline.

33
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:27,960
He reorganized my layers, and he reminded me to export every file in the right format.

34
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:31,880
If he hadn't done that, the developer wouldn't have been able to use my assets,

35
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:33,960
and we would have lost another week.

36
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:37,000
In the end, the client loved the new version.

37
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,320
She even said it was better than she had imagined.

38
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:42,760
Still, I can't stop thinking about the first mistake.

39
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:47,080
If I had taken the time to listen, I wouldn't have wasted so much energy.

40
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:49,320
Now, before every project,

41
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:51,000
I ask for a clear brief,

42
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,600
I look at the brand guidelines,

43
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:54,160
and I show early sketches.

44
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:57,440
Otherwise, I know I will repeat the same mistake.
